### Real-World Use Cases: The Decision Matrix

Let's look at 7 common app scenarios and see exactly which database wins.

| Use Case | Winner | Why? |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Banking & Financial Ledger** | **SQL** | You need exact transactions (ACID). You absolutely cannot have duplicate or mismatched money counts. |
| **E-commerce Store** | **SQL** | Products, Orders, Customers, Inventory, and Reviews all link together. You need `JOIN`s and strict data integrity. |
| **Employee Management System (HR)** | **SQL** | Highly structured data (Employee, Department, Salary, Roles) with lots of complex reports. |
| **Social Media News Feed** | **NoSQL** | Millions of users posting unstructured text, photos, and videos. You need to scale horizontally to handle the global load. |
| **Real-time Analytics / IoT Sensors** | **NoSQL** | Ingesting billions of small data points (temperature, speed, logs) every second. You don't need to link them; you just need to store them fast. |
| **Blog / Content Management** | **NoSQL** | Blog posts, comments, and tags can be nicely nested into a single Document (JSON). It's easy to scale read traffic. |
| **Inventory Management System** | **SQL** | Inventory tracking requires strict stock counts, warehouses, and complex ordering history. Data must be consistent. |

